    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "02411a41960aedae6564ceb6dca9d7bba0ad9f81b7a0ee0a4555cda3c253e348",
      "text": "Spend a full day exploring Iguazú National Park on the Argentine side. The waterfall system has 275 cascades surrounded by subtropical forest. The name “Iguazú” comes from Guaraní and means “big water.”\n\nThe highlight is the 72-meter-high Garganta del Diablo, or Devil’s Throat. The park’s rich plant and animal life makes the journey to the falls part of the experience. Take the ecological train through the park, then follow the walkways and viewing platforms on the Upper and Lower Circuits. Each section offers a different perspective, from views above the water to paths that take you closer to the lower cascades.\n\n**Iguazú Great Adventure: Zodiac boat and jungle**\n\nThe optional Great Adventure excursion costs $100 per person.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw6lz405-1ivofn2o2t2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
    },
